      en: ["Knockalongy is the highest peak in the Ox Mountains at 544 meters.", "The rock consists of Pre-Cambrian gneiss, which is over 600 million years old.", "The mountains were formed during the Caledonian orogeny millions of years ago.", "Lough Talt is a significant glacial lake located within the mountain range.", "Large parts of the mountains are protected as Special Areas of Conservation (SAC).", "The region supports rare blanket bog ecosystems and threatened bird species."],
